best_ideas:
Further safeguards:
- a 513 unwind guard;
- country-less triples left unarmed;
- the survivor read two ways (the GBNHS<P> merged holder and nhs_body_survivor_now) and held to agreement;
- exact parity for a small hand-read cohort.

fatal_flaws:
The alias ordering fails:
- the gated NHS fallback runs only on an org_of MISS, so a refused mention's mint claims the triple, and every later mention binds that carrier by exact triple, whichever body it names;
- the re-read's G2 then refuses to re-merge the carrier, so the split regrows and mixes;
- the 'open' tier binds name-blind and is cached in org_of, steering any mis-publisher under a child code into the ICB;
- Tie passes both G2 and the gated bind.

